  m_Name: Cap4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Upper Rear Cap
  description: The Upper Rear Cap is a tiny but vital component located at the middle-center-rear
    of the jet engine, playing a crucial role in maintaining the engine's structural
    integrity and stability. Its compact design and high-strength material, such
    as Shaft1 2, enable it to withstand the high stresses and loads generated by
    the engine's operation. The Upper Rear Cap works in conjunction with other caps
    to provide a secure and stable mounting point for the engine's shaft and transmit
    power to the turbine.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6637f78b041daea4da6d06213b0388a6, type: 3}
